# The Gateway API implementation of the opt-in profile `TROVE_GATEWAY=1` (deploy/dev/up.sh, R-HA-038, R-HA-039): Envoy Gateway, the one
# R-HA-038 and R-HA-039 name, with the Gateway API CRDs of its chart (the standard channel with BackendTLSPolicy, HTTPRoute timeouts and the
# policies of R-HA-039). The chart is an OCI artifact (oci://docker.io/envoyproxy/gateway-helm): deploy/dev/lib.sh oci_chart_tgz pulls it once
# and checks the archive against the SHA-256 below on every use. The controller image and the Envoy proxy image (the chart's own defaults,
# pinned by digest) move together with the chart version; up.sh refuses a pin whose tag differs from the version.
# renovate: datasource=docker depName=docker.io/envoyproxy/gateway-helm
DEV_ENVOY_GATEWAY_CHART_VERSION=v1.10.0
DEV_ENVOY_GATEWAY_CHART_SHA256=0f72c9050c33dbaab39b865e8cb5ed77f263720b22368eda4ce687077649e659
DEV_ENVOY_GATEWAY_IMAGE=docker.io/envoyproxy/gateway:v1.10.0@sha256:c2243d43518bed91d3ed8c2db849a4b7a14ac9b96eb019f2ab104bb1ca8572b1
